<p>I really like this. Articles that use the real life horrors human history is replete with are too scarce in my opinion. But I do have a few nitpicks.</p>
<p>For one thing, the third interview log still has a few XXXXs that haven’t been removed yet. The last one is missing a few line breaks towards the end. Finally, though it is far more subjectively an error, I vociferously object to using “4196” as a stand-in for the proper term “SCP-4196” in the interview logs. I mean, we wouldn’t dream of doing that in the description or containment procedures, would we?</p>
<p>Speaking of the containment procedures, I don’t think the idea that continuously monitoring the corpses will root SCP-4196 in one place is quite justified. Why exactly that would help is not mentioned elsewhere in the article, and it is especially strange as the rest of the containment procedures seem to say that this is the first time SCP-4196 has shifted positions and that the Foundation is just waiting it out.</p>

